<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muroma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muroma were a Finnic people of the middle Oka basin, mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> among the peoples paying tribute to the Rus'. The town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murom">Murom</a> took its name from them. They were gradually assimilated by East Slavic settlers by the 11th and 12th centuries, and their burial grounds have yielded rich bronze ornaments.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muroma.jpg" alt="Muroma" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Finno-ugrian-map.png: Chesnok Finno-ugrian-map.svg: Urutseg derivative work: Karland90 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finno-ugrian-map-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
